On another SM8750 device, the virtio-gpu thread of a crosvm guest
entered reclaim from the kvmalloc() in the submit ioctl, and a
virtio-blk thread from an ext4 write.  Both were found in the same
wait when the guest stopped responding:

   dma_fence_default_wait+0x1fc/0x230
   dma_fence_wait_timeout+0xbc/0xfc
   dma_resv_wait_timeout+0x78/0x134
   active_evict+0x28/0x80
   drm_gem_lru_scan+0x114/0x2c4
   msm_gem_shrinker_scan+0x108/0x248
   ...
   __kvmalloc_node_noprof+0x27c/0x56c
   msm_ioctl_gem_submit+0x28c/0x1760

Signal completed hw fences from msm_gpu_retire() again, which runs from
the irq handler, the hangcheck timer and the recover worker.  The
completed fence is still updated first and unconditionally, so the race
fixed by that commit does not come back.  Then ring->submits is walked
under submit_lock, and fences are signalled in order up to the first
submit that is not complete.  This nests the fence lock inside
submit_lock, as update_fences() did.  retire_submits() still does the
cleanup, but fence signalling no longer waits for it.

Fixes: 3c7a52217a8c ("drm/msm: Drop update_fences()")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -850,13 +850,46 @@ static void retire_worker(struct kthread_work *work)
 	retire_submits(gpu);
 }
 
-/* call from irq handler to schedule work to retire bo's */
+/*
+ * Signal the hw_fence of each submit the GPU has completed, in ring order.
+ *
+ * This must not depend on retire_submits(), which takes the reservation lock
+ * of each BO of a submit: dma_fence_wait() may be called with a reservation
+ * lock held (by the shrinker, for example), and that waiter would then block
+ * the signalling of the fence it waits for.
+ */
+static void signal_completed_submits(struct msm_ringbuffer *ring)
+{
+	struct msm_gem_submit *submit;
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&ring->submit_lock, flags);
+	list_for_each_entry(submit, &ring->submits, node) {
+		/*
+		 * Submits on a ring complete in order, so stop at the first
+		 * one that is not complete.  dma_fence_is_signaled() signals
+		 * the fence when msm_fence_signaled() reports it complete.
+		 */
+		if (!dma_fence_is_signaled(submit->hw_fence))
+			break;
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ring->submit_lock, flags);
+}
+
+/*
+ * call from irq handler to signal completed fences, and schedule work to
+ * retire bo's
+ */
 void msm_gpu_retire(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	int i;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < gpu->nr_rings; i++)
-		msm_update_fence(gpu->rb[i]->fctx, gpu->rb[i]->memptrs->fence);
+	for (i = 0; i < gpu->nr_rings; i++) {
+		struct msm_ringbuffer *ring = gpu->rb[i];
+
+		msm_update_fence(ring->fctx, ring->memptrs->fence);
+		signal_completed_submits(ring);
+	}
 
 	kthread_queue_work(gpu->worker, &gpu->retire_work);
 }
